## Control {{controlId}}: Define, Document, Approve, and Enforce Access Restrictions Associated with Changes to Organizational Systems

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization enforces access restrictions for system changes within the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through role-based access control, Privileged Identity Management, and configuration change authorization managed by {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}.

{{#if roleAssignmentsConfigured}}
**Role-Based Change Authorization:**
{{roleAssignmentsCount}} role assignments define who can make configuration changes to the CUI environment:
{{#if assignments}}
{{#each assignments}}
- **{{principalDisplayName}}** — Role: {{roleDefinitionName}} (Scope: {{scope}})
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Only personnel with designated administrative roles can modify system configurations. Changes are restricted to the minimum scope required for the authorized modification.
{{else}}
Privileged role assignments for change authorization have not been confirmed.
{{/if}}

{{#if pimConfigured}}
**Just-in-Time Change Access:**
PIM enforces time-bound, approval-gated access for configuration changes:
{{#if policies}}
{{#each policies}}
- **{{roleDisplayName}}** — Approval required: {{#if approvalRequired}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}, MFA required: {{#if mfaRequired}}Yes{{else}}No{{/if}}, Max duration: {{activationDuration}}
{{/each}}
{{/if}}

Administrators must activate privileged roles through PIM before making system changes, creating an auditable approval chain for every configuration modification.
{{else}}
PIM has not been configured. Change access restrictions rely on static role assignments.
{{/if}}

**Responsible Party:** {{variables.accessControlAdministrator}}

**Verification Method:** Examine role assignment reports, PIM activation logs, change authorization records, and Entra ID audit logs for configuration modifications.

